l,\n      \"sha256\": \"089221fb9d7eee532f91c6ef40a4bfdaaa18c00fcc28bc2f538ddd6b6e3ff03e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"specification/REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"00a91bb5a16ba8802cb2d3132c08677c978f3ef50d4e6c61d864c5afdb960baa\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"15300e9871b842cb6ab81b360fe9717766638e82abc2d1cf06c5cebc2febfca3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"stdo_skills.json\",\n      \"root\": \"product\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"4339a7dbc735052c08962154966fc13a4e30206d42ba2e80b53c6009a5008c22\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"claude/PREDICATES.md\",\n      \"root\": \"successor\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"7753acef3a52d4e8ae15bf2c2d2ce8d0bbab80626d3c0f2edc8127cfac1c3e66\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"claude/HOST.md\",\n      \"root\": \"successor\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"cdd34bf4c1b18d43ff1f922367c282959f579aa4384583fb21513bf90a3d8408\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n      \"object\": null,\n      \"path\": \"claude/HISTORY.json\",\n      \"root\": \"successor\",\n      \"selector\": null,\n      \"sha256\": \"b413c8218d7b68e498a73065028f239e7c559eead5065a5406e71441f129bb74\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"root_paths\": {\n    \"host_claude\": \"/Users/jim/.local/share/claude/versions\",\n    \"host_codex\": \"/opt/homebrew/lib/node_modules/@openai/codex/node_modules/@openai/codex-darwin-arm64/vendor/aarch64-apple-darwin/bin\",\n    \"host_python\": \"/opt/homebrew/Cellar/python@3.13/3.13.7/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.13/bin\",\n    \"method\": \"/Users/jim/Library/Application Support/STDO/releases/v3.0.1-rc.1\",\n    \"operator\": \"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator\",\n    \"product\": \"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills\",\n    \"successor\": \"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/successor-1\",\n    \"tool\": \"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/a_c\"\n  },\n  \"tool_profile\": {\n    \"engine\": \"workspace-regular-file\",\n    \"object\": null,\n    \"path\": \"build_tenants/graphify/design/fd-method-stdo-3.0.1.json\",\n    \"root\": \"tool\",\n    \"selector\": null,\n    \"sha256\": \"a886047e50b8a45c3b47addea0f0809dca2a6c54ac35948df5e01893cc30bbf7\"\n  }\n}\n\n\n===== r-reqreadme specification/requirements/README.md =====\nRC0\n# Shared requirements\n\nStatus: common construction candidate. Applies equally to Codex and Claude.\nEach tenant traces these obligations to its own design, implementation and\n[scenario evidence](SCENARIOS.md); no identical skill decomposition is required.\nThe exact method owners are indexed in [SOURCE_OWNERS.md](../SOURCE_OWNERS.md).\n\n## SK-01: Discoverable task entry\n\nIn a declared supported host installation, ordinary relevant task requests must\nmake the applicable capability discoverable without requiring the user to remember\nthe skill name. Explicit invocation must work too. Descriptions distinguish\ngoverned development from unrelated work. Discovery is tested separately from\nwhether a loaded skill completes the task. Host limits and observed failures are\nreported instead of claiming guaranteed model compliance.\n\n## SK-02: Static basis and scope\n\nThe selected Product Definition and exact installed method are resolved and\nverified before relying on their contracts. Ambiguous, missing or altered bases\nwithhold dependent work. A moving selector, sibling source or retained summary\ncannot replace the pin. Setup installs or pins only within the supplied grant;\nordinary execution never adopts a newer cut implicitly.\n\n## SK-03: Lawful intake and proportional work\n\nThe skill identifies the required outcome, changed owner and applicable existing\nwork basis, then performs the smallest sufficient authorized work. A small direct\ntask does not automatically acquire a ticket, coordinating actor or reviewer.\nMaterial coordination and independent assessment are activated when their actual\nconditions require them. Existing sufficient authorization is reused without a\nrepeated permission ceremony; missing material authority remains explicit.\n\n## SK-04: Supported tool use\n\nEach selected operation has an exact implementation, input/output contract and\nsupported method binding. A declared required tool is actually called; its\nobserved response and effects support the resulting claim. The skill does not\nreplace its outcome with invented checks, a narrative of intended calls, or an\nunqualified alternate path. Pure construction, assessment, authority and F_P\nresults retain their distinct contracts under 3.0.1.\n\nCompatibility is established per operation. A legacy acquisition may supply\nopaque source bytes under its actual contract; an unsupported lifecycle profile\ncannot issue 3.0.1 admission or join results by relabeling. A tool failure preserves\npartial evidence and unknown effects, withholds the dependent claim and identifies\nthe next supported re-entry. Independent useful work may continue within its grant.\n\n## SK-05: Adequate bounded context\n\nContext retains the exact outcome, subject/basis, material relations, authority,\nrequired evidence, capability limits, return consumer and invalidators needed for\nthe task. It is acquired through current source routes and may use verified\nderived views. Equal candidate bytes do not erase differing retained assessments,\nunresolved obligations or currentness facts that require different continuations.\nNo general optimal-compression claim follows from a sufficient task context.\n\n## SK-06: Construction and delegated return\n\nDirect or delegated workers receive the governing requirement/design, exact\noperation grant and territory, applicable proof predicates and bounded return.\nDelegation preserves these bindings across the actual host handoff. A child\ncompletion does not start an unrequested stage. Actor output, transport success,\ncandidate availability, assessment and acceptance remain distinguishable.\n\n## SK-07: Independent review\n\nWhere required, the reviewer derives expectations from governing sources before\nevaluating the exact candidate and proof. The reviewer reports actual exposure,\nevidence, severity and affected claims; it does not author the adopted repair or\nassume acceptance authority. A different role label alone proves no independence.\nRequired fresh assessment after material change cannot be replaced by a stale\nreview result.\n\n## SK-08: Continuation and recovery\n\nOn resume or interrupted execution, acquire material current state and reconcile\nobserved effects before retry. Retain unresolved obligations and valid evidence;\ninvalidate only affected reliance with its reason. Distinguish no assessment,\nperformed indeterminate assessment and incomplete construction. A timeout does\nnot prove rollback, and a repeated request must not duplicate an uncertain effect.\n\n## SK-09: Truthful status and closure\n\nStatus names what was constructed, assessed and decided, including exact subject,\nbasis, evidence and remaining work. Closure follows applicable predicates and\nrequired dispositions, not test count, review occurrence or a fluent summary.\nAn unsupported or unperformed case remains visible, never a passing result.\n\n## SK-10: Release and installation\n\nRelease skills bind the exact selected candidate, release conditions, publication\ngrant and destination, using the supported release tools. They can prepare a\nreviewable release without inferring publication authority. They preserve the\nmethod's immutable-cut semantics and keep installation/adoption decisions explicit.\nInstallation into one host must not silently enable the other tenant or change\nunrelated user configuration. An upgrade retains the ability to identify the\nprevious package and deliberately replace or remove the selected installation.\n\n## SK-11: Independent realization and maintenance\n\nEach tenant declares its requirements-to-algorithms and algorithms-to-host\nbindings, supported versions, failure behavior and qualification scope. Shared\nmechanics are consumed rather than reimplemented without a supported distinction.\nTuning is driven by observed task behavior. Host changes, tool-contract changes\nand method adoption identify affected tests and claims without resetting unrelated\nvalid evidence. Skill/source references remain resolvable in the delivered form.\n\n## SK-12: Evidence and benefit\n\nQualification uses common task semantics, independent expected outcomes and the\nactual public host/tool paths. Retain actual invocation, acquired inputs, outputs,\ntool traces, observed effects, elapsed time and reported token/cost data; unavailable\nmeasures remain unknown. Compare equivalent substantive information and count\nretries, repair and review in total cost. One passing trial is bounded evidence,\nnot statistical reliability or general benefit. Keyword and formatting checks\nmay establish structure but not successful method application.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9069a765-b3ee-4a03-8f71-6288ce3b57b6","uuid":"19f236b9-0796-4d7f-af53-a18da4d74f1b","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:05:51.525Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"===== r-routes claude/SOURCE-ROUTES.json =====\nRC0\n{\n  \"deciding_method\": [\n    {\n      \"engine\": \"workspace-