{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S4vTPPKGiVsa1TKGdsdtt6","type":"tool_result","content":"===== claude/HOST.md =====\n# Claude host mechanics\n\nVerified local version: Claude Code 2.1.306. Configured fable/high remains inherited; actual resolution is recorded only from the run.\n\nOfficial documentation inspected 2026-10-25: [Extend Claude with skills](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills). Repository skills live in .claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md. Project skill search includes parents up to the worktree root. Description supplies automatic selection; /skill-name explicitly invokes the entry. Default invocation permits both user and model. disable-model-invocation:true removes automatic selection and is not selected here. Optional frontmatter and supporting files can specialize mechanics. Plugin skills use a namespace; names can collide across project/personal/plugin scopes, so verify the actual selected path. Some newer documented behavior requires versions after 2.1.306; do not assume it applies. This task selects a repository-local install first and requires actual discovery evidence.\n\nTenant algorithm and prompt design remain your own; this file is sourced host input, not a donor design. Your construction host exposes Bash and Read. Public CLI is the ordinary transport; no MCP approval is required. Scoped mkdir and read-only focused validation are authorized; file contents must use work.write.\n\n\n===== claude/HISTORY.json =====\n{\n  \"current_pid_observation\": {\n    \"argv\": [\n      \"ps\",\n      \"-p\",\n      \"96875\",\n      \"-o\",\n      \"pid=,comm=\"\n    ],\n    \"meaning\": \"Recorded direct PID absent; no universal descendant/effect absence claim\",\n    \"returncode\": 1,\n    \"stdout\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"decision\": \"New contract after known parent closure and observed absence of candidate writes. No replay of old dispatch or automatic retry. Keep external/descendant effects unknown where not observed.\",\n  \"direct_parent\": {\n    \"ended_ns\": 1792892588796580000,\n    \"failure\": \"nonzero parent exit or incomplete input/output transport\",\n    \"input_bytes\": 95486,\n    \"input_forwarded_bytes\": 95486,\n    \"output_available\": false,\n    \"pid\": 96875,\n    \"returncode\": 1,\n    \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.actor-cli-observation/1\",\n    \"started_ns\": 1792892587622421000,\n    \"stderr_bytes\": 0,\n    \"stderr_eof\": true,\n    \"stdout_bytes\": 5780,\n    \"stdout_eof\": true,\n    \"termination_requests\": [],\n    \"unknowns\": [\n      \"descendant/process-tree end and external side effects\",\n      \"host/model active-context size\",\n      \"backend retries or unreported usage\",\n      \"semantic outcome and owner disposition\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"failure\": {\n    \"observed\": \"Not logged in; Please run /login\",\n    \"reported_cost_usd\": 0,\n    \"reported_input_tokens\": 0,\n    \"reported_output_tokens\": 0,\n    \"standing\": \"No model-produced candidate or assessment. Selected environment repair restores only credential routing; future authentication success unobserved.\"\n  },\n  \"original_process\": {\n    \"path\": \"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/claude/actor-cli-output/process.json\",\n    \"sha256\": \"5d9b4d947568152b58b45d1bb9da8af3cf5f52990595a12e66b07a399a6c35cb\"\n  },\n  \"prior_attempt\": {\n    \"id\": \"sha256:8e519a7970d602e7d96f0732104e5c5801567739124641c3781aad3b75d9d1ef\",\n    \"sha256\": \"8e519a7970d602e7d96f0732104e5c5801567739124641c3781aad3b75d9d1ef\"\n  },\n  \"retained_observations\": [\n    {\n      \"effect\": {\n        \"core_value\": \"indeterminate\",\n        \"end_established\": false,\n        \"process_end_established\": true,\n        \"residuals\": [\n          \"Generic process/return does not establish intended semantic outcome or all external/descendant effect end.\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"completion_unknown\"\n      },\n      \"evidence\": {\n        \"id\": \"sha256:3e28fec022ddeb701be697a4786b1e4c04a2675b325dd82662e98cdb1addec37\",\n        \"sha256\": \"3e28fec022ddeb701be697a4786b1e4c04a2675b325dd82662e98cdb1addec37\"\n      },\n      \"output\": {\n        \"observed_bytes\": {\n          \"stderr\": 96,\n          \"stdout\": 0\n        },\n        \"process_end\": {\n          \"descendants\": \"unknown\",\n          \"ended_ns\": 1792892589122868000,\n          \"observed\": true,\n          \"returncode\": 1\n        },\n        \"stderr\": {\n          \"id\": \"sha256:0da9bf9970ad258ab1cc73cee59abc9d8eede20a6777e917229f13b35a95ef42\",\n          \"sha256\": \"0da9bf9970ad258ab1cc73cee59abc9d8eede20a6777e917229f13b35a95ef42\"\n        },\n        \"stdout\": {\n          \"id\": \"sha256:2dbfaa277a63b6b52715414b8f8485b27e424a2083dc4a08fbfd0bb36edc62a9\",\n          \"sha256\": \"2dbfaa277a63b6b52715414b8f8485b27e424a2083dc4a08fbfd0bb36edc62a9\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"process_end\": {\n        \"descendants\": \"unknown\",\n        \"ended_ns\": 1792892589122868000,\n        \"observed\": true,\n        \"returncode\": 1\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"effect\": {\n        \"core_value\": \"indeterminate\",\n        \"end_established\": false,\n        \"process_end_established\": true,\n        \"residuals\": [\n          \"Generic process/return does not establish intended semantic outcome or all external/descendant effect end.\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"completion_unknown\"\n      },\n      \"evidence\": {\n        \"id\": \"sha256:2a60535f362688b59f3794b6f4757c2bbc6725d7f128744240e8d59ba3322432\",\n        \"sha256\": \"2a60535f362688b59f3794b6f4757c2bbc6725d7f128744240e8d59ba3322432\"\n      },\n      \"output\": {\n        \"observed_bytes\": {\n          \"stderr\": 96,\n          \"stdout\": 0\n        },\n        \"process_end\": {\n          \"descendants\": \"unknown\",\n          \"ended_ns\": 1792892589122868000,\n          \"observed\": true,\n          \"returncode\": 1\n        },\n        \"stderr\": {\n          \"id\": \"sha256:0da9bf9970ad258ab1cc73cee59abc9d8eede20a6777e917229f13b35a95ef42\",\n          \"sha256\": \"0da9bf9970ad258ab1cc73cee59abc9d8eede20a6777e917229f13b35a95ef42\"\n        },\n        \"stdout\": {\n          \"id\": \"sha256:2dbfaa277a63b6b52715414b8f8485b27e424a2083dc4a08fbfd0bb36edc62a9\",\n          \"sha256\": \"2dbfaa277a63b6b52715414b8f8485b27e424a2083dc4a08fbfd0bb36edc62a9\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"process_end\": {\n        \"descendants\": \"unknown\",\n        \"ended_ns\": 1792892589122868000,\n        \"observed\": true,\n        \"returncode\": 1\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n\n===== specification/SOURCE_OWNERS.md =====\n# Source owners\n\nAll method references below resolve within the immutable STDO v3.0.1-rc.1\ninstallation selected in `stdo_skills.json`, manifest\n`60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\nThis index routes acquisition; it does not duplicate the clauses or establish\nthat an operation has met them.\n\n| Concern | Deciding source within `standards/` |\n|---|---|\n| Exact Product and installed basis | PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§2, 4, 7, 9, 12 |\n| WHAT/HOW separation and tenant binding | SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 11; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §8 |\n| Intake, operation scope, admission and applicability | ACTIVATION.md §1 |\n| Context sufficiency, currentness and acquisition | ACTIVATION.md §2; REFERENCE_FRAME.md §§3, 11 |\n| Result, exhaustion, effects and disposition | ACTIVATION.md §3; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §§5, 7 |\n| Role configuration and bounded Executive decisions | EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md §§6, 8–10, 12, 16–19 |\n| Independent review and acceptance | EVALUATION.md §§3, 5, 7 |\n| Restart, retained results and invalidation | ACTIVATION.md §§5, 7; FOUNDATIONS.md observation sufficiency |\n| Cost and proportionality | ACTIVATION.md §6 |\n| Design and algorithm/computation binding | DESIGN_MODULE.md; SPEC_METHOD.md §§2, 10–11 |\n| Work carriers and condition-based closure | TICKETS.md §§5, 7 |\n| Actual-path proof and test semantics | ASSURANCE.md §§7–9; EVALUATION.md §7 |\n| Release identity and consumer adoption | RELEASE.md; IDENTITY.md |\n\nTenant designs add exact host/tool source references and their verified versions.\nHost documentation supplies mechanics and cannot alter these methodological\ncontracts. Existing STDO plugin skills and a_c examples are realization donors,\nwith their own declared support limits.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9069a765-b3ee-4a03-8f71-6288ce3b57b6","uuid":"b834d5f0-800b-4997-ba6f-c0e199300498","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:06:43.155Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"===== claude/HOST.md =====\n# Claude host mechanics\n\nVerified local version: Claude Code 2.1.306. Configured fable/high remains inherited; actual resolution is recorded only from the run.\n\nOfficial documentation inspected 2026-10-25: [Extend Claude with skills](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills). Repository skills live in .claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md. Project skill search includes parents up to the worktree root. Description supplies automatic selection; /skill-name explicitly invokes the entry. Default invocation permits both user and model. disable-model-invocation:true removes automatic selection and is not selected here. Optional frontmatter and supporting files can specialize mechanics. Plugin skills use a namespace; names can collide across project/personal/plugin scopes, so verify the actual selected path. Some newer documented behavior requires versions after 2.1.306; do not assume it applies. This task selects a repository-local install first and requires actual discovery evidence.\n\nTenant algorithm and prompt design remain your own; this file is sourced host input, not a donor design. Your construction host exposes Bash and Read. Public CLI is the ordinary transport; no MCP approval is required. Scoped mkdir and read-only focused validation are authorized; file contents must use work.write.\n\n\n===== claude/HISTORY.json =====\n{\n  \"current_pid_observation\": {\n    \"argv\": [\n      \"ps\",\n      \"-p\",\n      \"96875\",\n      \"-o\",\n      \"pid=,comm=\"\n    ],\n    \"meaning\": \"Recorded direct PID absent; no universal descendant/effect absence claim\",\n    \"returncode\": 1,\n    \"stdout\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"decision\": \"New contract after known parent closure and observed absence of candidate writes. No replay of old dispatch or automatic retry. Keep external/descendant effects unknown where not observed.\",\n  \"direct_parent\": {\n    \"ended_ns\": 1792892588796580000,\n    \"failure\": \"nonzero parent exit or incomplete input/output transport\",\n    \"input_bytes\": 95486,\n    \"input_forwarded_bytes\": 95486,\n    \"output_available\": false,\n    \"pid\": 96875,\n    \"returncode\": 1,\n    \"schema\": \"a_c.fd-support.actor-cli-observation/1\",\n    \"started_ns\": 1792892587622421000,\n    \"stderr_bytes\": 0,\n    \"stderr_eof\": true,\n    \"stdout_bytes\": 5780,\n    \"stdout_eof\": true,\n    \"termination_requests\": [],\n    \"unknowns\": [\n      \"descendant/process-tree end and external side effects\",\n      \"host/model active-context size\",\n      \"backend retries or unreported usage\",\n      \"semantic outcome and owner disposition\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"failure\": {\n    \"observed\": \"Not logged in; Please run /login\",\n    \"reported_cost_usd\": 0,\n    \"reported_input_tokens\": 0,\n    \"reported_output_tokens\": 0,\n    \"standing\": \"No model-produced candidate or assessment. Selected environment repair restores only credential routing; future authentication success unobserved.\"\n  },\n  \"original_process\": {\n    \"path\": \"/Users/jim/src/apps/specification_methodology-skills/stdo_skills/.ai-workspace/work/T001/operator/claude/actor-cli-output/process.json\",\n    \"sha256\": \"5d9b4d947568152b58b45d1bb9da8af3cf5f52990595a12e66b07a399