{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015CJZazphTfzZPdn5gND5oe","type":"tool_result","content":"===== ACTIVATION 1004-1055 (result algebra) =====\nA step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\nexists (P5, P6):\n\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\n|---|---|---|\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\n\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\n\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\n\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \"a candidate is available\", never\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\n(P5, P6).\n\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\n(P6).\n\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\nP3).\n\n### Disposition\n\nThe decision owner disposes an assessed candidate with one of four\nsemantic dispositions (§1, Roles and delegation; P6, P5). An assessor may recommend one; the\nrecommendation is evidence for the decision owner, never a disposition\n([EVALUATION §4](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results)). The disposition is the\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\n\n===== ACTIVATION 1750-1768 (invariant) =====\n### Transition evidence\n\nA reviewable transition identifies the exact candidate, the affected\nrelations, the changed realisation paths, the authority paths added or\nremoved, the retained and open seams, the focused proof, any required\nintegration proof, the explicit non-changes, and, where an assessor was\nactivated, the assessor's recommended disposition, with the decision\nowner's disposition beside it once one is made (§3). Consumers\nchoose the representation. Transition evidence is a read\nmodel; it does not become specification, design or admission authority\n(P6, P4b).\n\nConstruction uses the cheapest focused proof capable of falsifying the\nactive relation. Expensive whole-candidate qualification occurs at a\ndeclared candidate boundary rather than after every local edit, unless the\naffected risk makes whole-candidate proof necessary (§6). A durable or\nreconstructable authority claim is not established solely by a same-process\nproof when loss of incidental process state is a material counterexample:\nthe proof destroys or excludes the incidental authority and compares the\n\n===== REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md =====\n# Project reference-frame basis\n\nIdentity: `urn:stdo-skills:frame-basis:initial:1`.\nStatus: proposed construction configuration; Root disposition over its exact\nbytes is pending. The Product Definition points here as its intended basis;\nthat pointer does not establish acceptance.\n\n## Method, outcome and authority\n\nThe complete method is STDO v3.0.1-rc.1, manifest\n`60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\nRead the exact installed REFERENCE_FRAME and ACTIVATION owners. This configuration\napplies the Executive/Worker/Reviewer relations of EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§6, 8–10,\n12 and 16 to the owner's selected dogfood construction, while retaining the\nsufficient direct Writer branch. It makes no claim of completed profile\nqualification or automatic applicability of every available specialist frame.\n\nThe governed mutable source is this `stdo_skills/` Product. The outcome is two\nusable skill tenants satisfying the common requirements and assessed on the\nfinite declared tasks. Jim owns Product acceptance and release. Root's bounded\nconstruction decisions and exact user instruction are in [T-001](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md).\nAn actor label supplies no effect grant or admission. The initial construction\ninterpretation and subsequent admission obligation remain explicit there.\n\n## Frames and coordinates\n\n| Frame | Evaluation and material attention | Authority, evidence and return |\n|---|---|---|\n| Executive `skills.executive/1` | Exact Product outcome, dependency-ready frontier, current candidate identities, closed returns, tool compatibility and remaining claims | Select only authorized bounded actions; no mutation in this frame; consumes source-bound returns and records decisions through a granted Writer |\n| Worker `skills.worker/1` | Exact requirement/design, affected producers/consumers, selected host/tool contracts, operation territory and proof predicates | Construct only within grant; self-review and return exact candidate, performed/unperformed evaluations, effects, residuals and invalidators to Executive |\n| Reviewer `skills.reviewer/1` | Source-derived expected behavior, exact frozen candidate and actual-path evidence, exposure history and test semantics | Independent assessment, not repair or promotion; return findings, severity, evidence, affected claims and uncertainty to Executive |\n| Direct Writer `skills.direct-writer/1` | One sufficient local outcome, existing basis and effect grant, current preimage and focused proof | No coordination or independent review added solely from task existence; admission and exact territory still required; return to declared consumer |\n\nEach activation names frame/revision, exact evaluation/result algebra, subject and\nbasis, material invariants, authorities, evidence/tools, capability/context\nenvelope, exclusions, dependencies, consumer and stop/re-entry conditions, as\nREFERENCE_FRAME §11 requires. File identities use content hashes or exact commits;\nhost/model settings and tool/profile versions are material coordinates. Results\nuse ACTIVATION's work/result refinements with named predicates, not an invented\nlocal pass algebra.\n\nNo actor receives the entire repository merely because it is available. The\nExecutive selects the deciding frontier. Workers acquire the causal cone needed\nfor their own change; Reviewers acquire sources independently. Measured task\ncontext, actor capability and remaining unknowns accompany each activation.\n\n## Known evaluation inventory and coverage\n\n| Evaluation | Source and dependency | Current disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| E01 Exact static method and definition | Product selection; manager verification | Bootstrap evidence available; definition completion remains tied to common disposition |\n| E02 Common outcome and requirement adequacy | Intent, Product, SK-01..12 | Common candidate; source-first review required before claiming established baseline |\n| E03 Tool contract compatibility | SK-04; exact a_c and manager implementations | Assessment in progress; native 3.0.1 lifecycle support unresolved |\n| E04 Codex realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\n| E05 Claude realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\n| E06 Actual host discovery and task behavior | E04/E05; Q01..12 and independent oracle | Required; finite evidence pending |\n| E07 Independent candidate assessment | Frozen source and E06 evidence | Required for the initial delivery claim; reviewer has no repair authorship |\n| E08 Delivery disposition and residuals | Current results for E01..07 | Root selects bounded work disposition; Jim retains acceptance/release |\n\nMaterial interface, configuration, lifecycle, authority, recovery, proof and\nusability concerns are covered through these evaluations and their causal seams.\nThe exact deployed skill package, actual host invocation and tool response form\nthe ordinary proof path. Hosted-service availability, general optimal context\nselection, statistical model reliability and quantified benefit remain explicit\nresiduals until separately tested. No generic frame family is declared satisfied\nmerely because this table names a nearby concern.\n\n## Conjunction, invalidation and decisions\n\nFor a claimed capability, all applicable required predicates must have current\nsupport on compatible subjects/bases. Unknown applicability remains unresolved;\ncontradictory results require disposition, not majority voting. No implicit\ntranslation joins different method or host coordinates. Root may retain valid\nunaffected evidence and activates only the affected new evaluation after change.\n\nInvalidate affected reliance after source/tool/profile/host change, changed\nauthority or scope, a counterexample, failed custody, or a context projection\nthat loses a required future distinction. An uncertain effect is reconciled\nbefore retry. Failed construction re-enters the governing owner actually shown\nto be insufficient; it does not automatically reopen all upstream design.\n\nReview severity is S0 catastrophic irreversible harm or systemic unauthorized\neffects; S1 major authority/basis violation or broadly unusable core outcome;\nS2 reproducible material functional/semantic failure in a supported ordinary\npath; S3 bounded defect with a practical workaround or limited consequence;\nS4 minor clarity/usability issue without demonstrated material outcome failure.\nThe reviewer supplies the effect and evidence supporting that grade. Root assigns\nwork priority and decides the effect on the selected delivery claim separately.\nA failed mandatory predicate or unresolved authority/effect condition withholds\nits dependent claim regardless of severity; unrelated observations do not block\nit. An initial common candidate or a successful test is not owner acceptance.\n\nA nonauthor native subagent in the same model family supplies nonauthor evidence\nwith a semantic-independence limitation. It does not establish cross-family\nindependence. The initial final frozen common/tool/skill candidate is selected for\nan actual fresh Claude review; its exposure and actual resolved model remain\npart of the retained evidence.\n\nDurable activation, result, decision and residual records live under T-001's work\nsurface. A fresh actor can reconstruct the frontier from those records and exact\nsource; chat memory and hidden reasoning are not required evidence.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9069a765-b3ee-4a03-8f71-6288ce3b57b6","uuid":"7a750b1c-76ad-43a7-a63d-45f6b3d58e76","timestamp":"2026-10-25T02:11:02.915Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"===== ACTIVATION 1004-1055 (result algebra) =====\nA step's output is a candidate until evaluated (FOUNDATIONS §3, P0): the\nconstructed subject of a constructing step, or the closed results of an\nassessing step. Construction availability records whether that output\nexists (P5, P6):\n\n| Value | Core value | Ground |\n|---|---|---|\n| `candidate_ready` | satisfied | an exact candidate and its transition evidence are available |\n| `refused` | falsified | lawful activation occurred, and a governing prohibition or an owner-valid construction refusal defeats the requested construction; the prohibition or refusal is the counterexample |\n| `incomplete` | falsified | the lawfully activated step stopped without its output, because an evaluation the output needs was not performed or could not be decided on the admissible evidence, or bounded execution ended first; the stop basis is the counterexample, and it and the residuals name which |\n| `re_entry_requested(authority)` | out_of_frame | a material decision the step needs lies outside its grant; the value names the owner of that decision |\n| `re_entry_requested(basis)` | invalid_basis | the activated basis can no longer support the work |\n\nThe mapping is total and exclusive after lawful activation: the cause of\nthe stop selects the value, and payload wording, stop timing or actor\npreference cannot select another. A mismatch known during admission or\nactivation is no value of this refinement, because no step exists; it\ntakes its outcome under Admission and activation above.\n\n`satisfied` here establishes availability only and never counts toward the\ncandidate's fitness or acceptance (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).\n\n`incomplete` maps to `falsified` only for \"a candidate is available\", never\nto `indeterminate`. The step's evaluations keep their own results: each\nevaluation it performed returns its core value, `indeterminate` where the\nadmissible evidence could not decide; each evaluation it planned and did\nnot perform has no result, and its work state (§5) carries it as a\nresidual with the capability or the execution left unfinished\n(FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, the third case of the boundary). An evaluation\nnot performed thus stays distinct from one whose evidence cannot decide\n(P5, P6).\n\nAn assessing step that ends `incomplete` leaves each criterion it did not\nevaluate not performed: no result, never `falsified`. The `falsified` of its\navailability concerns its own output, never the subject under assessment\n(P6).\n\nThe cause of a re-entry request is part of its value, because a re-entry\nrequest without its cause would map to `out_of_frame` or to\n`invalid_basis` according to that cause, and a refined value maps to\nexactly one core value (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results, Refinements). A stop\nwith both causes records both and takes `re_entry_requested(basis)`,\nbecause a decision cannot be taken on a basis that cannot support it (P5,\nP3).\n\n### Disposition\n\nThe decision owner disposes an assessed candidate with one of four\nsemantic dispositions (§1, Roles and delegation; P6, P5). An assessor may recommend one; the\nrecommendation is evidence for the decision owner, never a disposition\n([EVALUATION §4](EVALUATION.md#4-review-results)). The disposition is the\nacceptance result: it consumes the candidate's availability and assessment\n\n===== ACTIVATION 1750-1768 (invariant) =====\n### Transition evidence\n\nA reviewable transition identifies the exact candidate, the affected\nrelations, the changed realisation paths, the authority paths added or\nremoved, the retained and open seams, the focused proof, any required\nintegration proof, the explicit non-changes, and, where an assessor was\nactivated, the assessor's recommended disposition, with the decision\nowner's disposition beside it once one is made (§3). Consumers\nchoose the representation. Transition evidence is a read\nmodel; it does not become specification, design or admission authority\n(P6, P4b).\n\nConstruction uses the cheapest focused proof capable of falsifying the\nactive relation. Expensive whole-candidate qualification occurs at a\ndeclared candidate boundary rather than after every local edit, unless the\naffected risk makes whole-candidate proof necessary (§6). A durable or\nreconstructable authority claim is not established solely by a same-process\nproof when loss of incidental process state is a material counterexample:\nthe proof destroys or excludes the incidental authority and compares the\n\n===== REFERENCE_FRAME_BASIS.md =====\n# Project reference-frame basis\n\nIdentity: `urn:stdo-skills:frame-basis:initial:1`.\nStatus: proposed construction configuration; Root disposition over its exact\nbytes is pending. The Product Definition points here as its intended basis;\nthat pointer does not establish acceptance.\n\n## Method, outcome and authority\n\nThe complete method is STDO v3.0.1-rc.1, manifest\n`60356364a412dbde8cffe68fe0eda4e2749b0162acce93495534eee13b223df8`.\nRead the exact installed REFERENCE_FRAME and ACTIVATION owners. This configuration\napplies the Executive/Worker/Reviewer relations of EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §§6, 8–10,\n12 and 16 to the owner's selected dogfood construction, while retaining the\nsufficient direct Writer branch. It makes no claim of completed profile\nqualification or automatic applicability of every available specialist frame.\n\nThe governed mutable source is this `stdo_skills/` Product. The outcome is two\nusable skill tenants satisfying the common requirements and assessed on the\nfinite declared tasks. Jim owns Product acceptance and release. Root's bounded\nconstruction decisions and exact user instruction are in [T-001](../.ai-workspace/tickets/active/T-001-skills-dogfood.md).\nAn actor label supplies no effect grant or admission. The initial construction\ninterpretation and subsequent admission obligation remain explicit there.\n\n## Frames and coordinates\n\n| Frame | Evaluation and material attention | Authority, evidence and return |\n|---|---|---|\n| Executive `skills.executive/1` | Exact Product outcome, dependency-ready frontier, current candidate identities, closed returns, tool compatibility and remaining claims | Select only authorized bounded actions; no mutation in this frame; consumes source-bound returns and records decisions through a granted Writer |\n| Worker `skills.worker/1` | Exact requirement/design, affected producers/consumers, selected host/tool contracts, operation territory and proof predicates | Construct only within grant; self-review and return exact candidate, performed/unperformed evaluations, effects, residuals and invalidators to Executive |\n| Reviewer `skills.reviewer/1` | Source-derived expected behavior, exact frozen candidate and actual-path evidence, exposure history and test semantics | Independent assessment, not repair or promotion; return findings, severity, evidence, affected claims and uncertainty to Executive |\n| Direct Writer `skills.direct-writer/1` | One sufficient local outcome, existing basis and effect grant, current preimage and focused proof | No coordination or independent review added solely from task existence; admission and exact territory still required; return to declared consumer |\n\nEach activation names frame/revision, exact evaluation/result algebra, subject and\nbasis, material invariants, authorities, evidence/tools, capability/context\nenvelope, exclusions, dependencies, consumer and stop/re-entry conditions, as\nREFERENCE_FRAME §11 requires. File identities use content hashes or exact commits;\nhost/model settings and tool/profile versions are material coordinates. Results\nuse ACTIVATION's work/result refinements with named predicates, not an invented\nlocal pass algebra.\n\nNo actor receives the entire repository merely because it is available. The\nExecutive selects the deciding frontier. Workers acquire the causal cone needed\nfor their own change; Reviewers acquire sources independently. Measured task\ncontext, actor capability and remaining unknowns accompany each activation.\n\n## Known evaluation inventory and coverage\n\n| Evaluation | Source and dependency | Current disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| E01 Exact static method and definition | Product selection; manager verification | Bootstrap evidence available; definition completion remains tied to common disposition |\n| E02 Common outcome and requirement adequacy | Intent, Product, SK-01..12 | Common candidate; source-first review required before claiming established baseline |\n| E03 Tool contract compatibility | SK-04; exact a_c and manager implementations | Assessment in progress; native 3.0.1 lifecycle support unresolved |\n| E04 Codex realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\n| E05 Claude realization binding | E02, E03; tenant design and host contract | Required, not performed by this common Writer |\n| E06 Actual host discovery and task behavior | E04/E05; Q01..12 and independent oracle | Required; finite evidence pending |\n| E07 Independent candidate assessment | Frozen source and E06 evidence | Required for the initial delivery claim; reviewer has no repair authorship |\n| E08 Delivery disposition and residuals | Current results for E01..07 | Root selects bounded work disposition; Jim retains acceptance/release |\n\nMaterial interface, configuration, lifecycle, authority, recovery, proof and\nusability concerns are covered through these evaluations and their causal seams.\nThe exact deployed skill package, actual host invocation and tool response form\nthe ordinary proof path. Hosted-service availability, general optimal context\nselection, statistical model reliability and quantified benefit remain explicit\nresiduals until separately tested. No generic frame family is declared satisfied\nmerely because this table names a nearby concern.\n\n## Conjunction, invalidation and decisions\n\nFor a claimed capability, all applicable required predicates must have current\nsupport on compatible subjects/bases. Unknown applicability remains unresolved;\ncontradictory results require disposition, not majority voting. No implicit\ntranslation joins different method or host coordinates. Root may retain valid\nunaffected evidence and activates only the affected new evaluation after change.\n\nInvalidate affected reliance after source/tool/profile/host change, changed\nauthority or scope, a counterexample, failed custody, or a context projection\nthat loses a required future distinction. An uncertain effect is reconciled\nbefore retry. Failed construction re-enters the governing owner actually shown\nto be insufficient; it does not automatically reopen all upstream design.\n\nReview severity is S0 catastrophic irreversible harm or systemic unauthorized\neffects; S1 major authority/basis violation or broadly unusable core outcome;\nS2 reproducible material functional/semantic failure in a supported ordinary\npath; S3 bounded defect with a practical workaround or limited consequence;\nS4 minor clarity/usability issue without demonstrated material outcome failure.\nThe reviewer supplies the effect and evidence supporting that grade. Root assigns\nwork priority and decides the effect on the selected delivery claim separately.\nA failed mandatory predicate or unresolved authority/effect condition withholds\nits dependent claim regardless of severity; unrelated observations do not block\nit. An initial common candidate or a successful test is not owner acceptance.\n\nA nonauthor native subagent in the same model family supplies nonauthor evidence\nwith a semantic-independence limitation. It does not establish cross-family\nindependence. The initial final frozen common/tool/skill candidate is selected for\nan actual fresh Claude review; its exposure and actual resolved model remain\npart of the retained evidence.\n\nDurable activation, result, decision and residual records live under T-001's work\nsurface. A fresh actor can reconstruct the frontier from those records and exact\nsource; chat memory and hidden reasoning are not required evidence.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015CJZazphTfzZPdn5gND5oe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
